#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:71
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:73
msgid ""
"Syncthing lets you synchronize your files bidirectionally across multiple "
"devices. This means the creation, modification or deletion of files on one "
"machine will automatically be replicated to your other devices. We believe "
"your data is your data alone and you deserve to choose where it is stored. "
"Therefore Syncthing does not upload your data to the cloud but exchanges "
"your data across your machines as soon as they are online at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:80
msgid ""
"The ``syncthing`` core application is a command-line program which usually "
"runs in the background and handles the synchronization. It provides a built-"
"in, HTML and JavaScript based user interface to be controlled from a web "
"browser. This frontend communicates with the core application through some "
"HTTP APIs, which other apps like graphical system integration helpers can "
"use as well, for greatest flexibility. A link to reach the GUI and API is "
"printed among the first few log messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:89
msgid "Common options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:93
msgid ""
"Set common configuration and data directory. The default configuration "
"directory is ``$XDG_STATE_HOME/syncthing`` or ``$HOME/.local/state/"
"syncthing`` (Unix-like), ``$HOME/Library/Application Support/Syncthing`` "
"(Mac) and ``%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Syncthing`` (Windows)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:101
msgid ""
"Set configuration directory. Alternative to ``--home`` and must be used "
"together with ``--data``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:106
msgid ""
"Set data (e.g. database) directory. Alternative to ``--home`` and must be "
"used together with ``--config``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:111
msgid ""
"Show help text about command line usage.  Context-sensitive depending on the "
"given subcommand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:115
msgid "Serve options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:119
msgid ""
"Try loading a config file written by a newer program version, instead of "
"failing immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:124
msgid "Write events to timestamped file ``audit-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.log``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:128
msgid ""
"Use specified file or stream (``\"-\"`` for stdout, ``\"--\"`` for stderr) "
"for audit events, rather than the timestamped default file name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:133
msgid ""
"Database maintenance interval -- internal database maintenance routines run "
"this often. The format is that of a Go duration string (see https://pkg.go."
"dev/time#ParseDuration)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:139
msgid ""
"Database deleted item retention interval -- deleted items are forgotten from "
"the database after this interval. The format is that of a Go duration string "
"(see https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:145
msgid ""
"Override GUI listen address. Set this to an address (``0.0.0.0:8384``) or a "
"URL (``http://0.0.0.0:8384``). Supported schemes are ``http`` for plain "
"HTTP, ``https`` for HTTP over TLS, ``unix`` for plain Unix sockets or "
"``unixs`` for TLS over Unix sockets. A Unix socket could look like this: "
"``unix:///run/syncthing/syncthing.socket`` (notice the three slashes: two as "
"part of the URL structure, one to specify an absolute path)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:154
msgid "Override the API key needed to access the GUI / REST API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:158
msgid ""
"Set destination filename for logging (use ``\"-\"`` for stdout, which is the "
"default option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:163
msgid ""
"Set the log level for all packages. Valid levels are DEBUG, INFO, WARN, and "
"ERROR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:168
msgid ""
"Number of old files to keep (zero to keep only current).  Applies only when "
"log rotation is enabled through ``--log-max-size``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:173
msgid "Maximum size in bytes of any log file (zero to disable log rotation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/syncthing.rst:177
msgid ""
"Format for timestamp, set to empty to disable timestamps. The format is that "
"of the Go time formatter (see https://pkg.go.dev/time#Layout)."
msgstr ""

